From f1cd16bf7bdd62d86cfb6a9f1553ada3f231d39c Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Gemini Mainline Project <noreply@invalid>
Date: Wed, 5 Aug 2026 17:25:23 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 159/159] arm64: add closed A72 transaction owner model

Add a lifecycle-closed, C-only owner layout for future MT6797 Cortex-A72 membership transactions. Keep the initial state explicitly UNINITIALIZED, retain a complete future transaction and fault ledger, and reject CPU8 and CPU9 probes before P31 or A38.

Provide read-only snapshots and default-off KUnit coverage proving that valid denials and token reads leave both the owner and dormant P30 model unchanged. The owner has no production caller or opener, cannot consume an attempt or mint a token, and cannot publish P30 or issue CPU_ON.

This experiment-only change has no certifying sign-off and is not submission-ready.
